Okay. I'm going to review this as a person who doesn't have any nostalgic attachment to the game. I didn't play it when it came out, I actually just got to play it now that it is on steam. That being said, this is also the opinion of a Sonic Fan who's been playing Sonic for nearly 18 years. Thing is SA2 just happened to never get to me, for some reason I wouldn't bother emulating it and never got to buy a Dreamcast.
So let's start. First of all, this game, like every Sonic game, has the germ of a good idea. When you TALK about Sonic Adventure 2 to someone who hasn't played it, it sounds amazing. Fast-paced, full of action, speed, attitude, good music and nice-ish graphics. What's not to love?
Still, SA2 has a lot of major problems.
- Glitches (too many for a finished game);
- Wacky controls;
- Poor level design;
- HORRIBLE camera;
- Really bad enemy placement;
- Bad arrangement between fast-paced and slow-paced stages;
- Bad story (not that big of a deal for a Sonic game, but it tries too hard to be plot-driven, you can't have bad plot if it's a focus on the game, period);
- The good stages are infested with scripted segments;
- and finally, 2/3 of the game is pure garbage. You HAVE to play as Tails, Knuckles, Rouge and Eggman to finish it, and it's atrocious.
It makes me so confused as to why people think this is one of the best, if not the best, Sonic game, when it clearly isn't. I don't like the heavy criticism the franchise has gone through since, idk, 2006 (and it's "revival" with game grumps), but this is NOT a good game. You can have fun with it, sure. The Sonic and Shadow stages aren't bad at all, they have some flaws, mainly the camera and controls and the scripted things, but when you get to REALLY play it and take control of the game, it's great (Metal Harbor would be the best example). But that's less than one third of the ENTIRE GAME.
Probably the best part about this mess isn't even the Sonic and Shadow stages, it's probably the Chao Garden.
Only waste your money on this if:
- You're nostalgic about it and can have fun with it even tho it's bad;
- You want to play the Chao Garden;
- You're a die hard Sonic Fan who just want to try every game.
Otherwise, you have a bunch of other options on Steam like Generations, the original trilogy & Knuckles, Sonic CD, the first Sonic Adventure. Hell! even Sonic Lost World is an okay game and more worth your money than this.
And if you want a really good 3D Sonic game just play the modern Generations Stages, or stay tuned for rumors saying Sonic Colors will be ported for PC.

